WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
Let’s talk about the assassination.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.560
Qassem Soleimani was seen as the second most powerful man in Iran.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.840
He was killed in Iraq 
when the Americans 

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.880
blew up his convoy using a drone.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.120
This is the equivalent of the 
Iranians assassinating  

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.160
the US secretary of defence.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.400
Iran is promising revenge.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.800
So who was Major General 
Qassem Soleimani?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.480
Why is there talk of a possible war between Iran and the US?

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.080
And was the attack even legal?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.880
I’m Sandra Gathmann. 

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.920
Welcome to a special 
episode of “Start Here”.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.960
You only have to look at the size of Qassem Soleimani’s funeral

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.720
to appreciate just how important 
he was to people in Iran.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.840
Soleimani was the leader of Iran’s powerful Quds Force.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.880
It’s the paramilitary wing of the Revolutionary Guard Corps

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.240
and it's active mostly outside of Iran.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.320
The US considers the force a 
terrorist organisation.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.280
The administrations of George W. 
Bush and Barack Obama

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.040
both considered assassinating Soleimani.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.880
Both rejected the option as too risky.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.440
Trump, though, pulled the trigger.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.600
Last Friday, Soleimani landed in Iraq, 
at Baghdad airport. 

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.720
He was with an Iraqi 
paramilitary commander 

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.760
named Abu Mahdi al Muhandis 
and other Iraqi officials.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.200
Circling somewhere high above 
them was a Reaper

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.640
a US military, remote-controlled 
killer drone.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.240
It’s unlikely they would have 
seen or heard it.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.960
To give you an idea of what 
these men were facing

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.120
here’s a video of a drone 
missile being tested. 

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.680
And here’s some amateur footage
 from Baghdad

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.280
that reportedly shows the actual 
missile strike on the convoy.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.240
They probably died instantly. 

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.640
Trump did not inform Congress 

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.800
about these plans to kill 
Soleimani in advance

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.440
This is very common for the Pentagon 

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.880
to present multiple military options 

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.720
to presidents in times of crisis. 

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.880
The Pentagon did not think, 
allegedly, that Trump

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.800
was going to select that option but
that is exactly what he did.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.360
So why strike now?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.480
The Trump administration says there was an imminent threat.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.360
It’s the only time an American president 

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.520
is allowed to order a military strike

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.360
on another country without congressional approval.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.200
We took action last night to stop a war.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.120
We did not take action to start a war.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.360
Under US law Trump had 48 hours 

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.640
to explain himself to Congress, 
in writing 

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.160
and he did, in a classified letter.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.120
But House Speaker Nancy Pelosi says

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.360
it raises more questions than answers.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.280
Democrats basically saying what is the evidence that you have?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.840
What is that intelligence? 

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.320
And so far the Trump administration 

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.440
is not wanting to release that publicly.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.760
The assassination of Qassem Soleimani didn’t just come out of nowhere.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.960
The US and Iran have been at each other for a while now.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.280
Starting with Trump’s decision in 2018 to pull out of the Iran nuclear deal.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.360
That led to the reimposition
 of US sanctions 

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.520
designed to cripple Iran’s economy.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.640
And Iran retaliated by resuming 
uranium enrichment.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.680
And ever since then there’s been trouble in the Gulf region. 

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.200
Iran was blamed for attacks 
on oil tankers.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.680
The Revolutionary Guard shot down 
a US surveillance drone.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.040
Then a Saudi oil refinery, the world’s biggest, was hit by a drone strike.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.120
Houthi rebels in Yemen said they did it but the US blames Iran.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.560
At the end of December the Americans bombed targets in Iraq and Syria

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.840
killing 25 militia fighters linked to Iran.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.840
That led to people storming the US embassy in Baghdad.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.640
And now the Soleimani assassination.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.960
The fallout from the assassination 
has been immediate.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.160
“The US is urging Americans to 
leave Iraq immediately

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.960
“The US is urging Americans to 
leave Iraq immediately

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.520
and is sending extra 
troops to the region 

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.960
in case of reprisal attacks.”

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.880
“Iran announcing it has no limits 
to its nuclear activity.”

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.440
Now, ever since the attack

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.720
there’s been speculation that Soleimani’s death

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.840
could lead to war between 
the US and Iran.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.360
But most observers don’t expect 
Iran will take that chance.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:59.960
The Iranian side is very clear that their conventional military power  

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:03.560
is dwarfed by that of the US, Israel 
and other regional allies  

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:08.760
of the US in the region but Iran has proven itself to be incredibly

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.640
sophisticated at asymmetric 
warfare, at cyberattacks.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.360
Right after Soleimani was killed 

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.800
the Americans were talking about de-escalating the situation.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.440
Then Trump tweeted.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.400
Basically warning Iran to 
forget about retaliating.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.640
Because if they did 

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.320
he’s already chosen 52 targets: 
one for each American  

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.720
held during the Iran hostage 
crisis in 1979.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.000
President Donald Trump has
 also been accused 

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.320
of ordering the assassination to 
distract the American public

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.640
from his impeachment proceedings.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.120
That was bound to happen.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.480
But whatever the motivation 

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:59.200
Donald Trump’s decision 
to kill Soleimani

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.160
has people around the world 
feeling a little less safe.

